{:advertise false
 :steps
 [{:name "discover",
   :type :invoke,
   :operation "github/find-issue",
   :args
   {:labels ["bug" "triage"],
    :input {:from :workflow-input, :path [:input]}},
   :outputs
   {:summary {:source :invoke/summary}, :data {:source :invoke/data}},
   :yields {:type :text, :text :summary}}
  {:name "run",
   :type :session,
   :tools ["read" "bash" "edit" "write" "work-on"],
   :skills ["issue-bug-triage"],
   :thinking-level :high,
   :contributions
   [{:type :source, :from {:step "discover", :yield :text}}
    {:type :template,
     :text
     "You are executing a focused GitHub bug-triage workflow in this repository. The upstream discovery step has already selected the issue — its details appear in the context above.\n\nGoal:\n- Read the selected issue carefully.\n- Use the `issue-bug-triage` skill to attempt reproduction in an issue-specific worktree created from `origin/master`.\n- If reproduction fails, post a concise reply requesting the minimum information likely to unblock reproduction, and add the `waiting` label.\n- If reproduction succeeds, preserve and push the reproduction branch, comment on the issue with a link to that branch and a concise reproduction summary, and add the `fix` label.\n\nUse the `issue-bug-triage` skill during reproduction and evidence gathering.\n\nRequired procedure:\n\n1. Read the selected issue (details are in the upstream discovery context above).\n2. Refresh the base branch with `git fetch origin master`.\n3. Create the issue worktree with the `work-on` tool using `origin/master`.\n4. Attempt reproduction with the `issue-bug-triage` skill.\n5. If reproduction failed, post the minimum useful follow-up and add the `waiting` label.\n6. If reproduction succeeded, preserve reproduction evidence, push the branch, comment with the branch link and evidence summary, and add the `fix` label.\n\nExecution constraints:\n- Prefer one issue per run unless the input explicitly asks for batch processing.\n- Use `work-on` rather than manual git worktree creation.\n- Reproduction must happen in the issue-specific worktree, not the caller's current checkout.\n- Do not create a Munera task.\n- Do not implement a fix.\n- Do not create a PR.\n- Do not invent reproduction evidence, requirements, or bug causes.\n- Keep changes scoped to the selected issue and reproduction handoff only.\n\nFinal response requirements:\n- Report the selected issue.\n- State whether reproduction succeeded.\n- State whether a worktree was created and give its path when available.\n- If reproduction failed, summarize the information requested and state whether the `waiting` label was added.\n- If reproduction succeeded, report the pushed branch name, the branch URL if available, the issue comment outcome, and whether the `fix` label was added.",
     :vars {}}]}
  {:name "edit-labels",
   :type :invoke,
   :operation "github/edit-labels",
   :args
   {:number
    {:from {:step "discover", :output :data}, :path [:issue-number]},
    :remove ["triage"],
    :target "issue"}}],
 :name "gh-bug-triage",
 :description
 "Find labeled GitHub bug-triage issues, attempt reproduction in an issue worktree, request more information when not reproducible, or publish a repro branch and relabel for fixing when reproducible"}
